  "worked_solution": "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{\u2015}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{\u2015}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (-9-5+3+8-1-4-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (-14) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [(-9)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{8}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-6)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [81+25+9+64+1+16+36] \\\\  & =\\frac{232}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{232}{7}-{(-2)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{232}{7}-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{232-28}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{204}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{204}{7}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{51}{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
